Package: marlinspike-agent
Version: __VERSION__
Section: net
Priority: optional
Architecture: all
Depends: python3 (>= 3.10), openssl
Recommends: marlinspike-capd
Maintainer: MarlinSpike Project <noreply@localhost>
Description: Remote sensor agent for MarlinSpike fleet management
 Enrolls with a central MarlinSpike fleet gateway over TLS and maintains
 an authenticated heartbeat connection. Relays live-capture control to a
 local capd sidecar and forwards each rotated capture's raw PCAP bytes
 upward over the same connection — the central fleet-gateway runs the
 actual analysis engine and produces the report; no analysis happens on
 this host. Zero third-party Python dependencies (stdlib ssl/asyncio
 only), no tshark or engine bundling needed.
 .
 Recommends marlinspike-capd (which itself pulls in wireshark-common /
 libpcap) so a plain `apt install ./marlinspike-agent*.deb` sets up a
 working sensor host in one shot — live capture relays to the local capd
 named in the Fleet page's start/stop calls, without a second manual
 install step. This agent still runs fine without it (relay-only host),
 just reporting capd_reachable: false / live capture unavailable.
